# Store every file byte-for-byte verbatim.
#
# Two reasons specific to this tree:
#   1. Source comments and identifiers are CP949/ANSI Korean, not UTF-8.
#      Byte-verbatim storage is the only way to leave those bytes alone.
#   2. Everything is CRLF from VS2003/VS2010. Any autocrlf guess would
#      produce a whole-file diff on every file in the repo.
#
# Do NOT add working-tree-encoding here to make Korean diffs readable --
# it rewrites file bytes on checkout. Mojibake in `git diff` is cosmetic.
* -text
